--TEST--
`Core\Router\Match::attribute<T>()` does not compile where one routed method has two attributes of the shape: `E0728` names the method, and a method with one match is not reported — `rule:routing/a-match-reads-an-attribute-as-data`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/shop", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[{limit: 10}]
    #[{limit: 20, label: "high"}]
    public function index(): void {}

    #[Core\Route(path: "/cart", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[{limit: 5}]
    public function cart(): void {}
}

?Core\Router\Match $shop = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/shop");
?{limit: int} $limit = $shop?->attribute<{limit: int}>();
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0728]: `Shop::index` has 2 attributes that match this shape
   --> case.nvs:16:24
   |
16 | ?{limit: int} $limit = $shop?->attribute<{limit: int}>();
   |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `attribute` returns at most one
   = help: add a field to the shape so that only one attribute of `Shop::index` has all of its fields

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
